== String conveniences in the style of Delphi's StrUtils (canon r3.64 module
== pairs). Compiler intrinsics, visible in a program that uses Std.StrUtils,
== which also gives everything of Std.Strings:
==
==   Trim(S String) String               == without White_Space at both ends
==   LTrim(S String) String              == ... at the start
==   RTrim(S String) String              == ... at the end
==   Left(S String, N Integer) String    == the first N characters, 0 <= N <= Length(S)
==   Right(S String, N Integer) String   == the last N characters
==   PadLeft(S String, Width Integer) String   == spaces before, up to Width characters
==   PadRight(S String, Width Integer) String  == spaces after
==   Replicate(S String, N Integer) String     == S repeated N times (Repeat is a keyword)
==   Replace(S String, Old String, New String) String  == every Old, left to right
==   Contains(S String, Sub String) Bool
==   StartsWith(S String, Prefix String) Bool
==   EndsWith(S String, Suffix String) Bool
==   SameText(A String, B String) Bool         == equal ignoring case
==   CompareText(A String, B String) Integer   == -1, 0 or 1 ignoring case
==
== White_Space and case follow Unicode, the same in every language.

Export Use Std.Strings
